  <title>5.2.6: Lesson Synthesis</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01254</md:content-id>
    <md:title>5.2.6: Lesson Synthesis</md:title>
    <md:uuid>be748a72-457d-4493-b75a-ad02acc7a712</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>In this lesson, students are introduced to the concept of roots above 2. They are also introduced to the concept that radicals can be written as terms with rational exponents.</para>
<para>Students may struggle with the properties for exponents when multiple properties are needed, for example, when negative exponents require an extra step.</para></section>
</content>
